.qwen/

# What the corpus left on disk before it moved into PostgreSQL: a Chroma store,
# the graph and the floor record under knowledge/, and the rebuild's lock file.
# Nothing writes them any more -- the corpus, its floor and the rebuild claim
# are all in the database -- but a checkout that ran an older console still
# has them, and they are one machine's data, never the repository's.
knowledge/chroma/
knowledge/knowledge_graph.json
knowledge/floor_calibration.json
knowledge.lock

# Last-run snapshot, written so a stopped or crashed run stays recoverable
# across a page reload. Per-machine runtime state, not history.
runs/

# Documents uploaded through the console. Whatever the operator handed this
# machine, not this project's source. Note that ignoring them here does not
# hide them from the corpus: the reindex walks the tree with glob, not git, and
# an upload is only durable because it is a file the walk finds.
uploads/

# Pages fetched by the online research phase. Third-party text this machine
# pulled down for a goal, not this project's source, and re-fetchable from the
# URL each one records in its header. Ignored here for the same reason uploads
# are, and with the same caveat: the walk is a glob, not git, so these are
# still indexed — which is the only thing that makes them survive a reindex.
research/web/

# Seat diagnostic output (scripts/diagnose_seats.py writes one timestamped
# directory per sweep). Per-run measurements against non-deterministic models,
# not history — the committed reports/*.md are written deliberately.
reports/diagnostics/

# An agent run's own write-ups — a machine inspection, an integration sketch, a
# brainstorm nobody finished. Per-run notes about one afternoon, not history,
# and never in the corpus, which reads only its archive roots.
experimental/

# Projects a run generated when the operator pointed it at one (the console's
# "where" dropdown). Separate products, not this project's source, and held out
# of the corpus until the operator embeds one (`langgraph_agent.projects`).
projects/

# Claude Code's per-machine permission grants, appended by the tool as it is
# used on this checkout. `.claude/` itself is tracked on purpose — the plan and
# the skills are project material — so only this one file is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# docker/install.sh's SearxNG config, with its secret key. (docker/.env is
# covered by .env above.)
docker/searxng/
